  "query_preview": "..Through tonight...A weak trough will quickly move \nto the east with a few lingering rain/show showers across the Four \nCorners through this afternoon and into the early evening. Snow \nlevels remain above 6000-6500 ft with little to no accumulation \nexpected. Otherwise, expect tonight to be dry with mostly clear \nskies and seasonably cold temperatures.\n\nTuesday through the weekend...Dry conditions are expected for the \nrest of the week and over the weekend. Temperatures will gradually \nwarm each day, becoming 5-10 degrees above average by Friday. Light \nnortheast to east winds 5-15 mph are expected on Tuesday, becoming \nvariable on Wednesday. Winds will shift from the north to northeast \non Thursday to southerly by Saturday as a weak, dry trough moves \nthrough the state. Winds will remain light through the end of the \nweek, around 5-15 mph each day. Another trough looks to move in over \nthe weekend but ensembles show this as remaining dry. The active \npattern looks to continue into next week but confidence remains low \nwith respect to precipitation chances.",
